# Design — Calm Mint Workspace

Taskory Hub UI for teams managing deadlines and assignments. Modern, friendly, mature — not childish. Prefer real workflows over showcase layouts.

## Direction

- Primary: mint/teal. Light canvas + soft pastels. Optional honey accent for **one** highlight per screen.
- Airy layout, clear hierarchy. Rounded cards, soft shadow, subtle gradient — sparingly.
- Decoration (sparkle, soft shapes): **empty states / hero only**, almost never on work chrome.
- Vary section scale/presentation; one clear visual anchor per screen.
- Responsive desktop → tablet → mobile (sidebar → bottom nav). Readable contrast always.

## Tokens (source of truth: `src/index.css`)

- Do not invent parallel color/font systems. Use CSS variables / Tailwind theme colors (`primary`, `secondary`, `muted`, `accent`, `destructive`, shadows).
- Typography: system UI stack (Unicode/UTF-8 via OS fonts). No custom webfonts unless product explicitly adds them.
- Icons: `lucide-react` only, consistent size/stroke.

## Components

- Prefer shadcn primitives; compose with `cn()`.
- Cards: use for interactive/grouped content; avoid identical card grids everywhere.
- Summary band / gradient hero: at most one per screen.
- Empty, loading, and toasts should feel on-brand (short personality) without cute overload. Errors stay clear (`toast` + `formatError`).

## Motion & states

- Hover/focus/active: light bg/border/opacity; focus ring = primary; 150–250ms ease.
- No strong glow, bounce on every card, or looping decorative animation on work screens.
- Loading: skeleton/spinner that preserves layout when possible.

## Anti-patterns

- Pink as dominant color; heavy gradient/shadow stacks; meaningless whitespace.
- Flat “template” dashboards with repeated identical cards.
- Hardcoded blue/purple theme hex when tokens already express mint/teal.
